{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fight for the Cause", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Second Conditional to talk about imaginary (hypothetical) or unreal situations in the present or future. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you have a million dollars?  No. <br> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really. <br>What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past verb + <span class=\"italic\">would</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"IF\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I went on an Arctic cruise, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be able to experience nature at its finest.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">an Arctic fox appeared,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would be very excited.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I were you,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would save a little money each month towards a cruise.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. You don't need a comma if the condition comes after the result in the sentence. <br><br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> I'd go on an Arctic cruise if I won the lottery tomorrow.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (I would = I'd.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": " If nobody cared about narwhals or any other animals in the world, there wouldn't be any animals left to care about!", "type": "example"}, {"content": " If I wanted to do that, I would buy a lottery ticket.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you really wanted to go, you could save enough in a few months. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Giving Advice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use modals to give advice. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The most common modals for giving advice are: <span class=\"italic\"> should</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can think of modals as \u201chelping verbs\u201d. They add meaning to the main verb of a sentence. In this case, these modals add the meaning of advice. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should</span> is the most common modal used to give advice.<br/><span class=\"italic\"> Ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span> are used for giving strong advice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Subject</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Modal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Main Verb</span>\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">should</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more about wildlife preservation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">ought to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">be</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more careful about disposing of your garbage.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> You</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">had better not</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">do</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">more to protect the whales.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<li>In conversation, it is common to use contractions with <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>.</li> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disconnected ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "removed from an issue; out of touch ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I feel so disconnected from the natural world.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about nature.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "documentary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a show or film that is factual and includes real-life events and people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I ought to watch more documentaries about wildlife.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Arctic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the area around the North Pole", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You could go on an Arctic cruise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "seal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a fish-eating mammal with a streamlined body and feet developed as flippers that lives in the ocean  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can see seals on an Arctic cruise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "polar bear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large, white bear found in the Arctic ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can see polar bears on an Arctic cruise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "walrus", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large mammal with two large tusks that lives in the Arctic Ocean ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: You can see walruses on your Arctic cruise.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Arctic fox", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small, white fox found in the Arctic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You might be able to see Arctic foxes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"